            <element name="DniDictDE1">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictDE1.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

D'ni to English Dictionary: A-I



<font style=n>Compiled by
Kh'reestrefah

Edited by
Korov'ev<PB>

<font style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb
<font size=12><PB>

<font style=b><p align=center>Sorting

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>The traditional D'ni alphabetical order is the following:

               V   B   T   S   SH
               J   G   Y   KH  K
               AH  AI  F   P   I
               EE  E   AY  R   M
               TH  DH  D   H   O
               OY  CH  W   UH  OO
               TS  L   A   Z   N

However, to make looking for terms easier, in this dictionary we adopted the common alphabetical order:

<font size=12 style=b>     <a href=#A>A<a link=clear>  <a href=#B>B<a link=clear>  <a href=#C>C<a link=clear>  <a href=#D>D<a link=clear>  <a href=#E>E<a link=clear>  <a href=#F>F<a link=clear>  <a href=#G>G<a link=clear>  <a href=#H>H<a link=clear>  <a href=#I>I<a link=clear>

<font size=10 style=n>Dnifont spellings are given in brackets: [Sora]. Tentative translations are marked with: (?).<PB><PB>

<a name=A><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>A<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>advuh<font size=10 style=n> [åDvu] (n.) arch.

<font size=10 style=b>-ah<font size=10 style=n> [-a] (suff.) imperative. Possibly also a superlative suff. (cf. <a href=#elahth>elahth<a link=clear>). 

<font size=10 style=b>ah<font size=10 style=n> [a] (prep.) marks an object directly affected by the action of the verb. Uses:
* in contrast with the recipient or goal
  marked by b';
* in contrast with the purpose marked by khe;
* when direct object is the subject of a
  subordinate clause.

<font size=10 style=b>ahbtsee<font size=10 style=n> [abxE] (n.) basalt.

<font size=10 style=b>ahbtsee-<a href=#ets>ets<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [abxEex] (adj.) basaltic.

<font size=10 style=b>ahchah<font size=10 style=n> [aca] (n.) sun(?), air(?), climate(?).

<font size=10 style=b>ahgo<font size=10 style=n> [ago] (adj./adv.) well.

<a name=ahl><font size=10 style=b>-ahl<font size=10 style=n> [-al] (suff.) verb to adjective ("-ing", "-ed").

<font size=10 style=b>ahl<font size=10 style=n> [al] (n.) branch(?), leaf(?), blossom(?), flower(?).

<a name=ahloth><font size=10 style=b>-ahloth<font size=10 style=n> [-aloT] (suff.) verb to noun (one who endures an action or state).

<a name=ahm><font size=10 style=b>-ahm<font size=10 style=n> [-am] (suff.) man(?), member(?). Telookahm "Surveyor".

<a name=ahn><font size=10 style=b>-ahn<font size=10 style=n> [-an] (suff.) augmentative or intensive ending in certain nouns, verbs, and adjectives describing extensive, thorough, or deep states or processes.

<font size=10 style=b>ahn<font size=10 style=n> [an] (n.) body of water(?).

<font size=10 style=b>ahnee<font size=10 style=n> [anE] (v.) become, get.

<font size=10 style=b>ahneem<font size=10 style=n> [anEm] (adj.) fluid.

<a name=ahno><font size=10 style=b>ahno<font size=10 style=n> [ano] (n.) water.

<font size=10 style=b>ahnoets<font size=10 style=n> [anoex] (adj.) watery, wet.

<font size=10 style=b>Ahno-nay<font size=10 style=n> [anonA] (n.) lit. "Water Root".

<font size=10 style=b>ahnotahm<font size=10 style=n> [anotam] (n.) lava; magma-based.

<a name=ahreeuh><font size=10 style=b>ahreeuh<font size=10 style=n> [arEu] (v.) protect.

<font size=10 style=b>ahreeuh-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [arEutan] (n.) protector.

<font size=10 style=b>ahreeuh-tahv<font size=10 style=n> [arEutav] (n.) protection.

<font size=10 style=b>ahro<font size=10 style=n> [aro] (adj.) other, different.

<font size=10 style=b>ahro-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [arotan] (n.) outsider, outworlder.

<font size=10 style=b>ahroy<font size=10 style=n> [arO] (v.) attend(?).

<font size=10 style=b>ahrtah<font size=10 style=n> [arta] (v.) allow(?), permit(?), let(?), do(?), cause(?).

<font size=10 style=b>ahtmay<font size=10 style=n> [atmA] (v.) stop(?), remove(?).

<font size=10 style=b>ahtsoo<font size=10 style=n> [axU] (adj.) ready.

<font size=10 style=b>ahve<font size=10 style=n> [ave] (n.) error.

<font size=10 style=b>ahyo<font size=10 style=n> [ayo] (n.) icon, symbol.

<font size=10 style=b>ahyo<a href=#heek>heek<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [ayohEK] (n.) D'ni game very similar to rock-paper-scissors. Historically the game was played with cane sticks marked with symbols.

<font size=10 style=b>Aitrus<font size=10 style=n> [Atrus] (n.) a D'ni name, actually spelled the same as Atrus.

<font size=10 style=b>al<font size=10 style=n> [ål] (n.) branch.

<font size=10 style=b>altee<font size=10 style=n> [åltE] (n.) branches.

<font size=10 style=b>altee rilerilonin<font size=10 style=n> [åltE rilerilonin] (n.) unexplored branches (cf. rilerilonin).

<font size=10 style=b>atinor<font size=10 style=n> [åtinor] (n.) beauty.

<font size=10 style=b>atinor-<a href=#et>et<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [åtinoret] (adj.) beautiful.

<font size=10 style=b>Atrus<font size=10 style=n> [Atrus] (n.) a D'ni name, actually spelled the same as Aitrus.

<font size=10 style=b>ayshoyk<font size=10 style=n> [ASOK] (v.) realize.

<font size=10 style=b>ayts'day<font size=10 style=n> [Ax'DA] (n.) retribution.


<a name=B><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>B<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>b<font size=10 style=n> [b-] (prep.) to.

<font size=10 style=b>bah<font size=10 style=n> [ba] (n.) beast.

<a name=#bahkh><font size=10 style=b>bahkh<font size=10 style=n> [bak] (adj.) baked(?) (cf. <a href=#chorbahkh>chor bahkh<a link=clear>).

<font size=10 style=b>bahn<font size=10 style=n> [ban] (n.) land(?).

<font size=10 style=b>bahntahno<font size=10 style=n> [bantano] (n.) island.

<font size=10 style=b>bahr<font size=10 style=n> [bar] craft(?), strength(?), energy(?).

<font size=10 style=b>bahrel<font size=10 style=n> [barel] (v.) make.

<font size=10 style=b>bahrel-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [bareltan] (n.) Maker, God.

<font size=10 style=b>bahrel-tahv<font size=10 style=n> [bareltav] (n.) (something) made.

<font size=10 style=b>bah'ro/bahro<font size=10 style=n> [ba'ro] (n.) bahro; beast-people, enslaved ahrotahntee.

<font size=10 style=b>bahron-<a href=#et>et<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [baronet] (adj.) phosphorescent.

<font size=10 style=b>bahrtah<font size=10 style=n> [barta] (v.) accomplish(?).

<font size=10 style=b>bahsh/bash<font size=10 style=n> [baS/båS] (v.) sense(?).

<font size=10 style=b>bahtsahnah<font size=10 style=n> [baxana] (n.) map.

<font size=10 style=b>bahtsen<font size=10 style=n> [baxen] (v.) map.

<font size=10 style=b>bahtsen-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [baxentan] (n.) cartographer.

<font size=10 style=b>bahvahn-<a href=#in>in<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [bavanin] (adj.) hidden.

<font size=10 style=b>bantee<font size=10 style=n> [båntE] (n.) series (seemingly always plural).

<font size=10 style=b>baykh<font size=10 style=n> [bAk] (v.) link, use a book to travel between Ages.

<font size=10 style=b>b'<a href=#bree>bree<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [b'brE] (quantif.) a little (lit. "to two").

<font size=10 style=b>be<font size=10 style=n> [be] (prep.) to.

<font size=10 style=b>beerah<font size=10 style=n> [bEra] (v.) keep, stay, remain.

<font size=10 style=b>beeree<font size=10 style=n> [bErE] (v.) maintain.

<font size=10 style=b>beeree-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [bErEtan] (n.) Maintainer.

<font size=10 style=b>bek<font size=10 style=n> [beK] (n.) game.

<font size=10 style=b>bekhe<font size=10 style=n> [beke] (v.) compel, force.

<font size=10 style=b>bel<font size=10 style=n> [bel] (v.) claim.

<font size=10 style=b>beletsahrah<font size=10 style=n> [belexara] (n.) plant similar to a lechuguilla agave.

<font size=10 style=b>bel'khah<font size=10 style=n> [bel'ka] (adj.) strange.

<font size=10 style=b>behn<font size=10 style=n> [ben] (prep.) for (exchange or duration).

<font size=10 style=b>bezol<font size=10 style=n> [bezol] (v.) trap.

<font size=10 style=b>bezol pumi<font size=10 style=n> [bezol pumE?] (n.) a carnivorous plant clinging on trees, native to Negilahn. Its preys are the pumi.

<font size=10 style=b>b'<a href=#fahsee>fahsee<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [b'fasE] (quantif.) as much as possible (lit. "to twenty-five").

<font size=10 style=b>bigto<font size=10 style=n> [bigto] (n.) blessing.

<font size=10 style=b>bintah<font size=10 style=n> [binta] (n.) law, ordinance.

<font size=10 style=b>birahno<font size=10 style=n> [birano] (n.) sea (cf. <a href=#ahno>ahno<a link=clear>). Birahnokh Rintotee "Sea of Dreams".

<font size=10 style=b>bishtah<font size=10 style=n> [biSta] (n.) tunnel.

<a name=biv><font size=10 style=b>biv<font size=10 style=n> [biv] (determ.) all, every.

<font size=10 style=b>biv-dil<font size=10 style=n> [bivDil] (pron.) everything.

<font size=10 style=b>biv-rov<font size=10 style=n> [bivrov] (pron.) everyone.

<a name=blo><font size=10 style=b>-blo<font size=10 style=n> [-blo] (num.) 25^5 (=9,765,625), combining form.

<font size=10 style=b>blo<font size=10 style=n> [blo] (prep.) about.

<a name=bo><font size=10 style=b>bo-<font size=10 style=n> [bo-] (pref.) simple fut. tense ("will write").

<a name=bodo><font size=10 style=b>bodo-<font size=10 style=n> [boDo-] (pref.) fut. prog. tense ("will be writing").

<a name=bodol><font size=10 style=b>bodol-<font size=10 style=n> [boDol-] (pref.) fut. perf. prog. tense ("will have been writing").

<a name=boko><font size=10 style=b>boko-<font size=10 style=n> [boKo-] (pref.) fut. perf. tense ("will have written") (see bol-). Perhaps intentional rather than predictive of a future state.

<font size=10 style=b>bol<font size=10 style=n> [bol] (n.) brother.

<a name=bol><font size=10 style=b>bol-<font size=10 style=n> [bol-] (pref.) fut. perf. tense ("will have written").

<font size=10 style=b>bonoo<font size=10 style=n> [bonU] (n.) acid.

<font size=10 style=b>bonoo-ets<font size=10 style=n> [bonUex] (adj.) acidic.

<font size=10 style=b>boogin<font size=10 style=n> [bUgin] (n.) creature.

<font size=10 style=b>bor<font size=10 style=n> [bor] (n.) page, specifically of the special paper used in Linking Books.

<font size=10 style=b>borin<font size=10 style=n> [borin] (adj.) tired.

<font size=10 style=b>bortah<font size=10 style=n> [borta] (n.) purpose(?).

<font size=10 style=b>bre-<font size=10 style=n> [bre-] (prep.) to the (b' + re-).

<a name=bree><font size=10 style=b>bree<font size=10 style=n> [brE] (num.) 2, two.

<font size=10 style=b>bren<font size=10 style=n> [bren] (n.) millennium.

<font size=10 style=b>b'rigahsen<font size=10 style=n> [b'rigasen] (quantif.) highly (lit. "to twenty-three").

<font size=10 style=b>b'rish<font size=10 style=n> [b'riS] (quantif.) so, very (lit. "to twenty").

<font size=10 style=b>broon<font size=10 style=n> [brUn] (n.) tube.


<a name=C><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>C<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>cannen<font size=10 style=n> [Kånen?] (n.) a device for playing recorded music.

<font size=10 style=b>chahg<font size=10 style=n> [cag] (v.) add.

<font size=10 style=b>chahn<font size=10 style=n> [can] (v.) can, be able to, may.

<font size=10 style=b>chay<font size=10 style=n> [cA] (n.) fault (geological).

<font size=10 style=b>cheecho<font size=10 style=n> [cEco] (n.) temperate grassland biome.

<font size=10 style=b>cheeree-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [cErEtan] (n.) animal native to Sameehn, undomesticated.

<font size=10 style=b>cheereelay<font size=10 style=n> [cErElA] (n.) animal native to Sameehn, domesticated.

<font size=10 style=b>cheto<font size=10 style=n> [ceto] (n.) disposition.

<font size=10 style=b>chev<font size=10 style=n> [cev] (n./v.) thank.

