<font size=10 style=b>prad-ets<font size=10 style=n> [pråDex] (adj.) rocky.

<font size=10 style=b>pradges<font size=10 style=n> [pråDges] (v.) sculpt.

<font size=10 style=b>pradges-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [pråDgestan] (n.) sculptor.

<font size=10 style=b>pradgestoy<font size=10 style=n> [pråDgestO] (n.) sculpture.

<a name=pradnuhreetee><font size=10 style=b>prad-<a href=#nuhree>nuhree<a link=clear>-tee<font size=10 style=n> [pråDnurEtE] (n.) money stone, "in essence like a modern smart card".

<font size=10 style=b>prad-teeg-ahl<font size=10 style=n> [pråDtEgal] (adj.) rock-working.

<font size=10 style=b>preniv<font size=10 style=n> [preniv] (adv.) once again.

<font size=10 style=b>prin<font size=10 style=n> [prin] (adj.) small.

<font size=10 style=b>prorahn<font size=10 style=n> [proran] (n.) unit of time equal to
1.5 seconds.

<font size=10 style=b>pumi<font size=10 style=n> [pumE?] (n.) a monkey-like animal native to Negilahn, usually jumping from tree to tree. Also known as "two tails monkey".]]></translation>
            </element>
            <element name="DniDictDE3">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictDE3.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

D'ni to English Dictionary: R-Z



<font style=n>Compiled by
Kh'reestrefah

Edited by
Korov'ev<PB>

<font style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb
<font size=12><PB>

<font style=b><p align=center>Sorting

<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>The traditional D'ni alphabetical order is the following:

               V   B   T   S   SH
               J   G   Y   KH  K
               AH  AI  F   P   I
               EE  E   AY  R   M
               TH  DH  D   H   O
               OY  CH  W   UH  OO
               TS  L   A   Z   N

However, to make looking for terms easier, in this dictionary we adopted the common alphabetical order:

<font size=12 style=b>     <a href=#R>R<a link=clear>  <a href=#S>S<a link=clear>  <a href=#T>T<a link=clear>  <a href=#U>U<a link=clear>  <a href=#V>V<a link=clear>  <a href=#W>W<a link=clear>  <a href=#X>X<a link=clear>  <a href=#Y>Y<a link=clear>  <a href=#Z>Z<a link=clear>

<font size=10 style=n>Dnifont spellings are given in brackets: [Sora]. Tentative translations are marked with: (?).<PB><PB>

<a name=R><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>R<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>r'<font size=10 style=n> [r'] (art.) the.

<font size=10 style=b>-rah<font size=10 style=n> [-ra] (num.) 25^2 (625), combining form.

<font size=10 style=b>rahm<font size=10 style=n> [ram] (adj.) good.

<font size=10 style=b>rahn<font size=10 style=n> [ran] (v.) vary(?).

<font size=10 style=b>rahnahl<font size=10 style=n> [ranal] (adj.) various.

<font size=10 style=b>rahshah<font size=10 style=n> [raSa] (adj.) dark(?).

<font size=10 style=b>rahshah-th<font size=10 style=n> [raSaT] (n.) dark, darkness.

<font size=10 style=b>rahsoo<font size=10 style=n> [rasU] (adj.) vanquished.

<font size=10 style=b>rahwah<font size=10 style=n> [rawa] (adj.) meaningful, rich :)

<font size=10 style=b>raiway<font size=10 style=n> [rIwA] (n.) procedure.

<font size=10 style=b>Rakeri<font size=10 style=n> [raKerE] (n.) a D'ni name.

<font size=10 style=b>ran<font size=10 style=n> [rån] (v.) measure.

<a name=re><font size=10 style=b>re-<font size=10 style=n> [re-] (art.) the/that.

<font size=10 style=b>Rebek<font size=10 style=n> [rebeK] (n.) lit. "The Game".

<font size=10 style=b>re'dahn-<a href=#tee>tee<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [re'DantE] (n.) long tweezers.

<font size=10 style=b>reekoo<font size=10 style=n> [rEKU] (n.) a small animal native to Ader Jamat.

<font size=10 style=b>reepah<font size=10 style=n> [rEpa] (n.) a timid, gorilla-like animal native to Negilahn, with a tail resembling a scorpion's. They eat nerim, gipeli and other plants and animals.

<font size=10 style=b>rees<font size=10 style=n> [rEs] (v.) eat.

<font size=10 style=b>reeslo<font size=10 style=n> [rEslo] (v.) dissolve.

<font size=10 style=b>reetahn<font size=10 style=n> [rEtan] (n.) survivor(?).

<font size=10 style=b>reethai<font size=10 style=n> [rETI] (prep.) during(?).

<font size=10 style=b>rek/rahk<font size=10 style=n> [reK/raK] (n.) class(?).

<font size=10 style=b>Relto<font size=10 style=n> [relto] (n.) lit. "the High Place" (re + el + <a href=#to>to<a link=clear>).

<a name=relyimah><font size=10 style=b>Relyimah<font size=10 style=n> [relyima] (n./adj.) Unseen, Terahnee slaves (cf. <a href=#rilyimah>rilyimah<a link=clear>, <a href=#yimah>yimah<a link=clear>).

<font size=10 style=b>rem<font size=10 style=n> [rem] (v.) flow.

<font size=10 style=b>remah<font size=10 style=n> [rema] (n.) north.

<font size=10 style=b>remesfet<font size=10 style=n> [remesfet] (adj.) diligent.

<font size=10 style=b>remesfet-eth<font size=10 style=n> [remesfeteT] (n.) diligence.

<font size=10 style=b>rev<font size=10 style=n> [rev] (n.) right (direction).

<font size=10 style=b>ri-<font size=10 style=n> [ri-] (num.) 20, twenty, combining form.

<font size=10 style=b>rifeen<font size=10 style=n> [rifEn] (v.) torment.

<a name=rifoon><font size=10 style=b>rifoon<font size=10 style=n> [rifUn] (v.) remember.

<font size=10 style=b>ri-gah-bree<font size=10 style=n> [rigabrE] (num.) 22, twenty-two.

<font size=10 style=b>ri-gah-fah<font size=10 style=n> [rigafa] (num.) 21, twenty-one.

<font size=10 style=b>ri-gah-sen<font size=10 style=n> [rigasen] (num.) 23, twenty-three.

<font size=10 style=b>ri-gah-tor<font size=10 style=n> [rigator] (num.) 24, twenty-four.

<font size=10 style=b>rigilahs<font size=10 style=n> [rigilas] (n.) taiga, boreal forest.

<font size=10 style=b>ril<font size=10 style=n> [ril] (determ.) no, not.

<font size=10 style=b>rilahsah<font size=10 style=n> [rilasa] (v.) unseal.

<font size=10 style=b>ril-dil<font size=10 style=n> [rilDil] (pron.) nothing.

<font size=10 style=b>rilerilonin<font size=10 style=n> [rilerilonin] (adj.) unexplored (cf. lon "discover"). Altee Rilerilonin "Unexplored Branches".

<font size=10 style=b>ril-gel-in<font size=10 style=n> [rilgelin] (adj.) unwritten.

<font size=10 style=b>ril-nahr<font size=10 style=n> [rilnar] (adj.) insignificant.

<font size=10 style=b>ril-rov<font size=10 style=n> [rilrov] (pron.) nobody.

<font size=10 style=b>ril-<a href=#tahgahm>tahgahm<a link=clear>-in<font size=10 style=n> [riltagamin] (adj.) unknown.

<font size=10 style=b>ril-<a href=#te>te<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [rilte] (prep.) without.

<a name=rilyimah><font size=10 style=b>rilyimah<font size=10 style=n> [rilyima] (adj.) unseen (cf. <a href=#relyimah>Relyimah<a link=clear>, <a href=#yimah>yimah<a link=clear>).

<font size=10 style=b>rinal<font size=10 style=n> [rinål] (v.) honor, venerate.

<font size=10 style=b>rinal-<a href=#tahv>tahv<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [rinåltav] (n.) honor, veneration(?).

<font size=10 style=b>rinto<font size=10 style=n> [rinto] (n.) dream. Birahnokh Rintotee "Sea of Dreams".

<font size=10 style=b>rish<font size=10 style=n> [riS] (num.) 20, twenty.

<font size=10 style=b>riway<font size=10 style=n> [rIwA] (n.) procedure.

<font size=10 style=b>ro'<font size=10 style=n> [ro'] (n., Terahnee) people group, household, or family (e.g. Hadre Ro'Jethhe).

<font size=10 style=b>robot<font size=10 style=n> [robot] (adj.) actual.

<font size=10 style=b>rochay<font size=10 style=n> [rocA] (v.) reach.

<font size=10 style=b>Ro-nay<font size=10 style=n> [ronA] (n.) lit. "People of the Root".

<font size=10 style=b>roo<font size=10 style=n> [rU] (conj.) that.

<font size=10 style=b>rooay<font size=10 style=n> [rUA] (n.) route.

<font size=10 style=b>rooayk<font size=10 style=n> [rUAK] (v.) destroy.

<font size=10 style=b>rooayk-<a href=#tahv>tahv<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [rUAKtav] (n.) destruction.

<font size=10 style=b>roob<font size=10 style=n> [rUb] (conj.) but.

<font size=10 style=b>roodsh<font size=10 style=n> [rUDS] (adj.) red.

<font size=10 style=b>roomay<font size=10 style=n> [rUmA] (v.) ignore(?), circumvent(?), alter(?).

<font size=10 style=b>roon<font size=10 style=n> [rUn] (num.) 0, zero.

<font size=10 style=b>roshee<font size=10 style=n> [roSE] (n.) crater.

<font size=10 style=b>rotee<font size=10 style=n> [rotE] (n.) peoples(?).

<a name=rov><font size=10 style=b>rov<font size=10 style=n> [rov] (n.) person.

<font size=10 style=b>rov-hoo<font size=10 style=n> [rovhU] (n.) holy person, saint (cf. hootsay "holy").


<a name=S><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>S<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>saheth<font size=10 style=n> [saeT] (n.) sleep.

<font size=10 style=b>say<font size=10 style=n> [sA] (n./v.) design.

<font size=10 style=b>sayrah<font size=10 style=n> [sAra] (n.) west.

<font size=10 style=b>se<font size=10 style=n> [se] (prep.) at.

<font size=10 style=b>-see<font size=10 style=n> [-sE] (num.) 25, combining form.

<font size=10 style=b>seen<font size=10 style=n> [sEn] (v.) get, acquire.

<font size=10 style=b>sek/sekh<font size=10 style=n> [seK/sek] (v.) have, own.

<font size=10 style=b>sel<font size=10 style=n> [sel] (v.) Write (Ages).

<font size=10 style=b>sel-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [seltan] (n.) Writer, one who writes Ages.

<font size=10 style=b>sen<font size=10 style=n> [sen] (num.) 3, three.

<font size=10 style=b>senahren<font size=10 style=n> [senaren] (n.) building, structure.

<font size=10 style=b>senper<font size=10 style=n> [senper] (adj.) triple, threefold.

<font size=10 style=b>seraht<font size=10 style=n> [serat] (v.) light up, brighten.

<font size=10 style=b>seren<font size=10 style=n> [seren] (n.) light.

<a name=serenol><font size=10 style=b>Serenol<font size=10 style=n> [serenol] (n.) Age where <a href=#tuliema>tuliema<a link=clear> grow, written by Atrus.

<font size=10 style=b>set<font size=10 style=n> [set] (pron.) us.

<font size=10 style=b>sev<font size=10 style=n> [sev] (n.) Age.

<a name=sh><font size=10 style=b>-sh<font size=10 style=n> [-S] (suff.) adjective to adverb ("-ly").

<font size=10 style=b>shahfee<font size=10 style=n> [SafE] (n.) span, equal to 15.8 ft or
4.82 m. Twice the length of a pendulum with a period of 5 prorahntee is 5 spans.

<a name=shahl><font size=10 style=b>shahl<font size=10 style=n> [Sal?] drop(?), extended below(?).
Tarpin shal, an animal native to Negilahn that preys by dropping down from high branches on unsuspecting victims.

<font size=10 style=b>shahmlis<font size=10 style=n> [Samlis] (adj.) perfect.

<font size=10 style=b>shahn<font size=10 style=n> [San] (v.) connect, piece together (as in a puzzle).

<font size=10 style=b>shahveroo<font size=10 style=n> [SaverU] (adj.) dire. Guhlem Shahveroo "Dire Strait".

<font size=10 style=b>sheegah<font size=10 style=n> [SEga] (n.) way(?), path(?), passage(?).

<font size=10 style=b>sheemah<font size=10 style=n> [SEma] (adj.) okay, alright.

<font size=10 style=b>sheetem<font size=10 style=n> [SEtem] (n.) message.

<a name=sheetemsootahn><font size=10 style=b>sheetemsoo-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [SEtemsUtan] (n.) messenger (sheetem + laysoo "carry").

<font size=10 style=b>sheeyah<font size=10 style=n> [SEya] (n.) angel.

<font size=10 style=b>Shegahdah<font size=10 style=n> [SegaDa] (n.) neighborhood in D'ni.

<font size=10 style=b>shelah<font size=10 style=n> [Sela] (v.) (tran)scribe(?).

<font size=10 style=b>shelah-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [Selatan] (n.) scribe.

<font size=10 style=b>shem<font size=10 style=n> [Sem] (pron.) you.

<font size=10 style=b>shento<font size=10 style=n> [Sento] (v.) take.

<font size=10 style=b>sheten<font size=10 style=n> [Seten] (v.) cherish.

<font size=10 style=b>shin<font size=10 style=n> [Sin] (adj.) able.

<font size=10 style=b>sho<font size=10 style=n> [So] (n.) dirt, soil.

<font size=10 style=b>shokhoo<font size=10 style=n> [SokU] (v.) instruct.

<font size=10 style=b>shokro-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [SoKrotan] (n.) bulldozer (lit. "dirt-mover").

<font size=10 style=b>shol<font size=10 style=n> [Sol] (v.) prepare.

<font size=10 style=b>sholen<font size=10 style=n> [Solen] (adj.) drawn.

<font size=10 style=b>shooth<font size=10 style=n> [SUT] (n.) death.

<font size=10 style=b>shorah<font size=10 style=n> [Sora] (n./interj.) peace; hello, farewell.

<font size=10 style=b>shorah-<a href=#T>t<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [Sorat] (adj.) peaceful.
Hahr rahm gah shoraht "happy new year"
(lit. "good and peaceful year").

<font size=10 style=b>shuhfay<font size=10 style=n> [SufA] (v.) finish.

<font size=10 style=b>shuhteejoo<font size=10 style=n> [SutEjU] (n.) rocksalt.

<font size=10 style=b>sifay<font size=10 style=n> [sifA] (adj.) wired.

<font size=10 style=b>sofeguh<font size=10 style=n> [sofegu] (v.) fear.

<font size=10 style=b>sol<font size=10 style=n> [sol] (n.) sister.

<font size=10 style=b>somah<font size=10 style=n> [soma] (n.) seal, signet.

<font size=10 style=b>soygi<font size=10 style=n> [sOgi] (adj.) stable.

<font size=10 style=b>soygish<font size=10 style=n> [sOgiS] mispelling of soygith.

<font size=10 style=b>soygi-th<font size=10 style=n> [sOgiT] (n.) stability.

<font size=10 style=b>stofah<font size=10 style=n> [stofa] of one.


<a name=T><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>T<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>-t<font size=10 style=n> [-t] (suff.) noun to adjective ("-ful") (cf. -et, -ets).

<font size=10 style=b>t'<font size=10 style=n> [t'] (prep.) in, by, with (cf. <a href=#te>te<a link=clear>, <a href=#terth>terth<a link=clear>-,
<a href=#tre>tre<a link=clear>-).

<font size=10 style=b>tah<font size=10 style=n> [ta] (pron.) it.

<font size=10 style=b>tahg<font size=10 style=n> [tag] (v.) give.

<a name=tahgahm><font size=10 style=b>tahgahm<font size=10 style=n> [tagam] (v.) know.

<font size=10 style=b>tahgayr<font size=10 style=n> [tagAr] (v.) learn.

<font size=10 style=b>tahgil<font size=10 style=n> [tagil] (v.) understand.

<font size=10 style=b>Tahgirah<font size=10 style=n> [tagira] (n.) a prison Age (possibly tahg + girah).

<font size=10 style=b>tahleeo<font size=10 style=n> [talEo] (n.) surface.

<font size=10 style=b>tahm<font size=10 style=n> [tam] (n.) fire.

<a name=tahn><font size=10 style=b>-tahn<font size=10 style=n> [-tan] (suff.) verb to noun ("-er", "-or", "-tor").

<font size=10 style=b>tahroo<font size=10 style=n> [tarU] (v.) die (by accident or murder).

<font size=10 style=b>tarpin <a href=#shahl>shal<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [tarpin Sal?] (n.) drop claw, an animal native to Negilahn that preys by dropping down from high branches on unsuspecting victims. Oocha para is a young tarpin shal. The tarpin shal life cycle is connected to the gahtsai.

<font size=10 style=b>tahs<font size=10 style=n> [tas] (v.) muse, think, ponder, meditate.

<a name=tahv><font size=10 style=b>-tahv<font size=10 style=n> [-tav] (suff.) verb to noun ("-ion", "-tion").

<font size=10 style=b>tahvo<font size=10 style=n> [tavo] (n.) unit of time equal to 14.5 min. Divided into 25 gorahntee.

<font size=10 style=b>Takotah<font size=10 style=n>, misspelling of <a href=#tokotah>Tokotah<a link=clear>.

<font size=10 style=b>tanuh<font size=10 style=n> [tånu] (v.) be blind(?), be injured(?).

<font size=10 style=b>tanuh-th<font size=10 style=n> [tånuT] (n.) blindness(?), injury(?).

<font size=10 style=b>tay<font size=10 style=n> [tA] (n.) aim(?), goal(?) (cf. taykheboorkh).

<font size=10 style=b>taygahn<font size=10 style=n> [tAgan] (v.) love.

<font size=10 style=b>taykheboorkh<font size=10 style=n> [tAkebUrk] (v.) seek. Taykheboorkhtahn Tsahvahn, "Eternal Seeker".

<font size=10 style=b>taynee<font size=10 style=n> [tAnE] (v.) welcome.

<font size=10 style=b>tayr<font size=10 style=n> [tAr] (v.) help.

<font size=10 style=b>tayroo<font size=10 style=n> [tArU] (adj.) apparent(?), thorough(?).

<font size=10 style=b>tayroo-<a href=#sh>sh<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [tArUS] (adv.) apparently(?) thoroughly(?).


<a name=te><font size=10 style=b>te<font size=10 style=n> [te] (prep.) by, with, in; of, among (cf. t', <a href=#terth>terth-<a link=clear>).

<a name=tee><font size=10 style=b>-tee<font size=10 style=n> [-tE] (suff.) plural ("-s").

<font size=10 style=b>-tee<font size=10 style=n> [-tE] (suff.) 2nd pers. plur. actor ("you").

<font size=10 style=b>tee'ahnah<font size=10 style=n> [tE'ana] (n.) story-teller. Ti'ana, D'ni name of Anna.

<font size=10 style=b>teeg<font size=10 style=n> [tEg] (v.) work.

<font size=10 style=b>teeg-ahl<font size=10 style=n> [tEgal] (adj.) working.

<font size=10 style=b>teeg-et<font size=10 style=n> [tEget] (adj.) working.

<a name=teegtahg><font size=10 style=b>teegtahg<font size=10 style=n> [tEgtag] (n.) study. Also used as a suffix ("-ology").

<font size=10 style=b>teeg-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [tEgtan] (n.) worker.

<font size=10 style=b>teeg-<a href=#tahv>tahv<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [tEgtav] (n.) work.

<font size=10 style=b>teejuh<font size=10 style=n> [tEju] (n.) squad(?).

<font size=10 style=b>teemah<font size=10 style=n> [tEma] (n.) south. Kotsah Teemah, "South Gate".

<font size=10 style=b>tefoonet<font size=10 style=n> [tefUnet] (n.) memorial (cf. <a href=#rifoon>rifoon<a link=clear>).

<font size=10 style=b>tel<font size=10 style=n> [tel] (n.) Guild.

<font size=10 style=b>tel-bahtsen<font size=10 style=n> [telbaxen] (n.) Guild of Cartographers (tel-okh bahtsen-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear>-tee).

<font size=10 style=b>tel-beeree<font size=10 style=n> [telbErE] (n.) Guild of Maintainers (tel-okh beeree-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear>-tee).

<font size=10 style=b>tel-betsiv<font size=10 style=n> [telbexiv] (n.) Guild of Engineers.

<font size=10 style=b>tel-dhoo'shol<font size=10 style=n> [telDU'Sol] (n.) Guild of Caterers (tel-okh doo'shol-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear>-tee).

<font size=10 style=b>Teledahn<font size=10 style=n> [teleDan] (n.) lit. "Place of Mushroomy Spores" (<a href=#to>to<a link=clear>-elemar-tee-nadahnets).

<font size=10 style=b>telensho<font size=10 style=n> [telenSo] (n.) Guild of Tour Guides (tel-okh lensho-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear>-tee).

<font size=10 style=b>tel-kailo<font size=10 style=n> [telKIlo] (n.) Guild of Healers.

<font size=10 style=b>tel-nahvah<font size=10 style=n> [telnava] (n.) Guild Master.

<font size=10 style=b>telook<font size=10 style=n> [telUK] (n.) Guild of Surveyors (<a href=#tel>tel<a link=clear> + look "survey").

<font size=10 style=b>telookahm<font size=10 style=n> [telUKam] (n.) Surveyor (telook + ahm).

<font size=10 style=b>telook-nahvah<font size=10 style=n> [telUKnava] (n.) Surveyors Guild Master.

<font size=10 style=b><a href=#tel>tel<a link=clear>-<a href=#rov>rov<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [telrov] (n.) guildsman.

<font size=10 style=b>telshee<font size=10 style=n> [telSE] (n.) Guild of Messengers (tel-okh <a href=#sheetemsootahn>sheetemsootahn<a link=clear>-<a href=#tee>tee<a link=clear>).

<font size=10 style=b>tem<font size=10 style=n> [tem] (n.) ordinary ink (cf. lem "ink for Linking Books").

<font size=10 style=b>temah<font size=10 style=n> [tema] (v.) hear(?), heed(?).

<a name=temo><font size=10 style=b>temo<font size=10 style=n> [temo] (prep.) after(?), since(?) (cf. <a href=#te>te<a link=clear> "by", mo "that").

<font size=10 style=b>ten<font size=10 style=n> [ten] (adj.) simple.

<font size=10 style=b>Te'negamiris<font size=10 style=n> [te'negamiris?] (n.) the great burial Age.

<font size=10 style=b>ten-esh<font size=10 style=n> [teneS] (adv.) simply.

<font size=10 style=b>ter<font size=10 style=n> [ter] (n.) tree. Terahnee "New Tree".
Terokh Jeruth "Tree of Possibility".
Garternay "Root of the Great Tree".

<font size=10 style=b>terelin<font size=10 style=n> [terelin] (n.) contact.

<a name=terth><font size=10 style=b>terth<font size=10 style=n> [terT] (prep.) in a, of a, as a (cf. <a href=#T>t'<a link=clear>, ehrth-).

<font size=10 style=b>tes<font size=10 style=n> [tes] (n.) group.

<font size=10 style=b>tetemo<font size=10 style=n> [tetemo] (prep.) onwards(?), afterwards(?) (cf. <a href=#te>te<a link=clear>, <a href=#temo>temo<a link=clear>).

<font size=10 style=b><a href=#te>Te<a link=clear>-<a href=#tsonot>tsonot<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [texonot] (n.) lit. "in (the) abyss".

<a name=th><font size=10 style=b>-th<font size=10 style=n> [-T] (suff.) adjective to noun ("-ty",
"... one") (cf. -eth).

<font size=10 style=b>thirk<font size=10 style=n> [TirK] (v.) save, keep.

<font size=10 style=b>thoe<font size=10 style=n> [Toe, ToE] (adv.) "how?". Possibly an alternate spelling of dho.

<font size=10 style=b>Ti'ana<font size=10 style=n> [tE'ana] (n.) story-teller; D'ni name of Anna.

<font size=10 style=b>tik<font size=10 style=n> [tiK] (v.) deny, refuse.

<font size=10 style=b>tikolee<font size=10 style=n> [tiKolE] (n.) (sorrow).

<font size=10 style=b>tikolee-<a href=#T>t<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [tiKolEt] (adj.) sorry.

<font size=10 style=b>tildah<font size=10 style=n> [tilDa] (v.) suffocate.

<font size=10 style=b>timel<font size=10 style=n> [timel] (n.) gallery.
Timelokh Kaydish "Kadish Gallery".

<font size=10 style=b>tishmah<font size=10 style=n> [tiSma] (n.) friend.

<font size=10 style=b>tiwah<font size=10 style=n> [tiwa] (n.) shaft.

<a name=to><font size=10 style=b>to<font size=10 style=n> [to] (n.) place. Often used as prefix meaning "place of" (cf. following entries).

<font size=10 style=b>to-delmer<font size=10 style=n> [toDelmer] (n.) planetarium
(to "place" + delahn "sky" + mer "to watch").

<font size=10 style=b>to-gitsah<font size=10 style=n> [togixa] (n.) haven
(to "place" + gitsah "safe").

<font size=10 style=b>togo<font size=10 style=n> [togo] (n.) floor.
Retogo kenen ahnoets "the floor is wet".

<font size=10 style=b>tokituh<font size=10 style=n> [toKitu] (v.) determine, be determined.

<a name=tokotah><font size=10 style=b>To-kotah<font size=10 style=n> [toKota] (n.) lit. "place of the locked door".

<font size=10 style=b>to-lesah<font size=10 style=n> [tolesa] (n.) sealed place, vault.

<font size=10 style=b>tomahgilo<font size=10 style=n> [tomagilo] (n.) garden (cf. tomahn, gilo "plant").

<font size=10 style=b>tomahn<font size=10 style=n> [toman] (n.) house (possibly to + mahn "existence").

<font size=10 style=b>tomahnah<font size=10 style=n> [tomana] (n.) home.

<font size=10 style=b>tomahrah<font size=10 style=n> [tomara] (n.) concert hall (cf. mahrah).

<font size=10 style=b>tome<font size=10 style=n> [tome] (adj.) homesick (lit. "out of place").

<font size=10 style=b>to-met<font size=10 style=n> [tomet] (adv.) here (lit. "this place").

<font size=10 style=b>to-mot<font size=10 style=n> [tomot] (adv.) there (lit. "that place").

<font size=10 style=b>tonah<font size=10 style=n> [tona] (adj.) long.

<font size=10 style=b>toogo<font size=10 style=n> [tUgo] (n.) foot.

<font size=10 style=b>tool<font size=10 style=n> [tUl] (v.) grow.

<font size=10 style=b>toomin<font size=10 style=n> [tUmin] (adj.) touched(?), handled(?), pressed(?).

<font size=10 style=b>to-porpah<font size=10 style=n> [toporpa] (n.) palace (cf. porpah "king").

<font size=10 style=b>tor<font size=10 style=n> [tor] (num.) 4, four.

<font size=10 style=b>toran<font size=10 style=n> [torån] (n.) unit of angular elevation, equal to 0.00576°; a right angle is 15,625 (25^3) torantee.

<font size=10 style=b>to-re-kor<font size=10 style=n> [toreKor] (n.) library (lit. "place of the book").

<font size=10 style=b>tor-ets<font size=10 style=n> [torex] (num.) fourth.

<font size=10 style=b>torinai<font size=10 style=n> [torinI] (adj.) cold.

<font size=10 style=b>torn<font size=10 style=n> [torn] (v.) spit.

<font size=10 style=b>to-<a href=#tel>tel<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [totel] (n.) Guild House.

<font size=10 style=b>tre-<font size=10 style=n> [tre-] (prep.) at the, in the, near the, with the, of the (cf. <a href=#T>t'<a link=clear>, <a href=#re>re<a link=clear>-).

<font size=10 style=b>Tre'biv-dil<font size=10 style=n> [tre'bivDil] (n.) lit. "in the everything".

<font size=10 style=b>trel<font size=10 style=n> [trel] (adj.) blue.

<font size=10 style=b>tren<font size=10 style=n> [tren] (determ.) a few, some.

<font size=10 style=b>trom<font size=10 style=n> [trom] (n.) wing.

<font size=10 style=b>trom-ets<font size=10 style=n> [tromex] (adj.) winged.

<font size=10 style=b>trov<font size=10 style=n> [trov] (v.) spin.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahn<font size=10 style=n> [xan] (adv.) always, forever.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahnlee<font size=10 style=n> [xanlE] (n.) mountain.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahnlee <a href=#yahm>yahm<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [xanlE yam] (n.) iceberg.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahno<font size=10 style=n> [xano] (adj.) everlasting, permanent, eternal (nonliving).

<font size=10 style=b>tsahno-<a href=#sh>sh<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [xanoS] (adv.) permanently.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahn-<a href=#ril>ril<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [xanril] (adv.) never (lit. "always not").

<a name=tsahr><font size=10 style=b>tsahr<font size=10 style=n> [xar] (v.) go.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahroo<font size=10 style=n> [xarU] (n./adj.) eye(?), full(?).

<font size=10 style=b>tsahv<font size=10 style=n> [xav] (v.) live.

<font size=10 style=b>tsahv-ahn<font size=10 style=n> [xavan] (adj.) immortal, eternal (living).

<font size=10 style=b>tsahv-<a href=#teegtahg>teegtahg<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [xavtEgtag] (n.) biology.

<font size=10 style=b>tsaydor<font size=10 style=n> [xADor] (v.) (burrow).

<font size=10 style=b>tsaydor-<a href=#tahn>tahn<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [xADortan] (n.) burrower, burrowing animal.

<font size=10 style=b>tseemah<font size=10 style=n> [xEma] (v.) need.

<font size=10 style=b>tseemah-ahl<font size=10 style=n> [xEmaal] (adj.) needed, necessary.

<font size=10 style=b>tso<font size=10 style=n> [xo] (prep.) of, about. Used to express non-personal relation.

<font size=10 style=b>tsofah<font size=10 style=n> [xofa] (n.) horn (of an animal).

<font size=10 style=b>tsogahl<font size=10 style=n> [xogal] (adj.) sunny, bright. Eder Tsogal, a Garden Age.

<font size=10 style=b>tsoid<font size=10 style=n> [xoiD] (v.) glow.

<font size=10 style=b>tsoid-ahl<font size=10 style=n> [xoiDal] (adj.) glowing.

<font size=10 style=b>tson<font size=10 style=n> [xon] (n.) (foundation).

<a name=tsonot><font size=10 style=b>tsonot<font size=10 style=n> [xonot] (n.) abyss (cf. Mayan tz'onot).
<a href=#te>Te<a link=clear>tsonot, lit. "in the abyss".

<font size=10 style=b>tsoonoo<font size=10 style=n> [xUnU] (v.) greet.

<font size=10 style=b>tsootay<font size=10 style=n> [xUtA] (v.) dedicate(?), owe(?).

<font size=10 style=b>tsosah-<a href=#tahv>tahv<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [xosatav] (n.) possession.

<font size=10 style=b>tsotoy<font size=10 style=n> [xotO] (n.) child.

<a name=tuliema><font size=10 style=b>tuliema<font size=10 style=n> [tuliema] (n.) a plant native to <a href=#serenol>Serenol<a link=clear>, with three leaves that thrust through the earth into the air and turn a bright yellow hue at dawn.


<a name=U><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>U<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>uhgraht<font size=10 style=n> [ugrat] (n.) pillars in the Riven wahrk lake, used to hung villagers to be fed to the wahrk as a form of punishment.

<font size=10 style=b>uru<font size=10 style=n> [UrU] (n.) large gathering; great community.

<font size=10 style=b>urwin<font size=10 style=n> [urwin?] (n.) a large animal native to Negilahn. Its primary food source is the kiri. The Payiferen 'sandscrit' is generally believed to be related to the urwin.


<a name=V><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>V<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>vah-<font size=10 style=n> [va-] (num.) 5, five, combining form.

<font size=10 style=b>vah-gah-bree<font size=10 style=n> [vagabrE] (num.) 7, seven.

<font size=10 style=b>vah-gah-fah<font size=10 style=n> [vagafa] (num.) 6, six.

<font size=10 style=b>vah-gah-sen<font size=10 style=n> [vagasen] (num.) 8, eight.

<font size=10 style=b>vah-gah-tor<font size=10 style=n> [vagator] (num.) 9, nine.

<font size=10 style=b>vahkh<font size=10 style=n> [vak] (adj.) linking (cf. korvahkh "Linking Book").

<font size=10 style=b>vahmo<font size=10 style=n> [vamo] (n.) east.

<font size=10 style=b>vahmo<font size=10 style=n> [vamo] (adj.) calm.

<font size=10 style=b>vahmo-<a href=#T>t<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [vamot] (adj.) eastern; pacific.

<font size=10 style=b>vaht<font size=10 style=n> [vat] (num.) 5, five.

<font size=10 style=b>vailee<font size=10 style=n> [vIlE] (n.) D'ni month, slightly longer than a Surface month. Divided into 29 <a href=#yahr>yahr<a link=clear>tee.

<font size=10 style=b>vaiuh<font size=10 style=n> [vIu] (n.) event(?), term(?).

<font size=10 style=b>vaynuh<font size=10 style=n> [vAnu] (v.) ask(?), explore(?).

<font size=10 style=b>vaytsoo<font size=10 style=n> [vAxU] (n.) presence.

<font size=10 style=b>veech<font size=10 style=n> [vEc] (v.) (scream).

<font size=10 style=b>veech-<a href=#tahv>tahv<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [vEctav] (n.) scream.

<font size=10 style=b>veelay<font size=10 style=n> [vElA] (n.) soul.

<font size=10 style=b>veewuh<font size=10 style=n> [vEwu] (v.) to deserve.

<font size=10 style=b>Venalem<font size=10 style=n> [venalem] (n.) ink-harvesting Age (cf. lem "ink").

<font size=10 style=b>veren<font size=10 style=n> [veren] (v.) mollify, pacify.

<font size=10 style=b>viduh<font size=10 style=n> [viDu] (n.) atmosphere.

<font size=10 style=b>vilekh<font size=10 style=n> [vilek] (n.) misery.

<font size=10 style=b>v'jah<font size=10 style=n> [v'ja] (n.) celebration (cf. Korfah V'ja "First Book Celebration").

<font size=10 style=b>vog<font size=10 style=n> [vog] (n.) nature.

<font size=10 style=b>vog-ets<font size=10 style=n> [vogex] (adj.) natural.

<font size=10 style=b>vokan<font size=10 style=n> [voKån] (n.) birth.

<font size=10 style=b>volah<font size=10 style=n> [vola] (interj.) yes.

<font size=10 style=b>voohee<font size=10 style=n> [vUhE] (aux. v.) can, could. Usually following the main verb: kenen voohee shuhteejoo "it could be rocksalt".

<font size=10 style=b>vor<font size=10 style=n> [vor] (n.) page (ordinary paper) (cf. bor "Linking Book page").

<font size=10 style=b>votahnah<font size=10 style=n> [votana] (n.) truth.

<font size=10 style=b>votahr<font size=10 style=n> [votar] (v.) praise.


<a name=W><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>W<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>winis<font size=10 style=n> [winis] (adv.) together.

<font size=10 style=b>wish<font size=10 style=n> [wiS] (v.) lift, raise.

<font size=10 style=b>wotsah<font size=10 style=n> [woxa] (adj.) harsh.


<a name=Y><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Y<p align=left>

<a name=yahm><font size=10 style=b>yahm<font size=10 style=n> [yam] (n.) ice

<a name=yahr><font size=10 style=b>yahr<font size=10 style=n> [yar] (n.) D'ni day, equal to 30 hr 14 min (1.26 Surface days). Divided into 5 gahrtahvotee.

<font size=10 style=b>Yahvo<font size=10 style=n> [yavo] (n.) Maker, God.

<font size=10 style=b>yayshah<font size=10 style=n> [yASa] (n.) joy.

<font size=10 style=b>yeepay<font size=10 style=n> [yEpA] (n.) eyeglasses, (goggles).

<font size=10 style=b>yeeshah<font size=10 style=n> [yESa] (n.) laughter.

<font size=10 style=b>yeret<font size=10 style=n> [yeret] (aux. v.) may. Usually following the main verb: Yahvo pilelen yeret veelayon "may Yahvo receive her soul".

<font size=10 style=b>yertis<font size=10 style=n> [yertis] (n.) a small plant native to Riven. Its yellow berries contain a neurotoxin used for hunting food.

<font size=10 style=b>yim<font size=10 style=n> [yim] (v.) see.

<a name=yimah><font size=10 style=b>yimah<font size=10 style=n> [yima] (adj.) seen.

<font size=10 style=b>yishah<font size=10 style=n> [yiSa] (n.) (planet).

<font size=10 style=b>yoorach<font size=10 style=n> [yUråc] (v.) breathe.

<font size=10 style=b>yootay<font size=10 style=n> [yUtA] (n.) guinea pig.

<font size=10 style=b>yootay<font size=10 style=n> [yUtA] (v.) owe.


<a name=Z><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Z<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>zahfay<font size=10 style=n> [zafA] (n.) fate.

<font size=10 style=b>zahg<font size=10 style=n> [zag] (v.) (prolong).

<font size=10 style=b>zahgah<font size=10 style=n> [zaga] (adj.) prolonged.

<font size=10 style=b>zander<font size=10 style=n> [zånDer] (n.) gravity.

<font size=10 style=b>zandni<font size=10 style=n> [zånDnE] (n.) Call to D'ni (zander + D'nee).

<font size=10 style=b>ze<font size=10 style=n> [ze] (pron.) her, him.

<font size=10 style=b>zeeglah<font size=10 style=n> [zEgla] (adj.) mad; insane, twisted, warped.

<font size=10 style=b>zeero<font size=10 style=n> [zEro] (n.) center(?), point of origin(?). Regahro Zeero "the Great Zero".

<font size=10 style=b>zeeway<font size=10 style=n> [zEwA] (n.) weather.

<font size=10 style=b>zik<font size=10 style=n> [ziK] (n.) (pod).

<font size=10 style=b>zintsahr<font size=10 style=n> [zinxar] (v.) escape(?), leave(?); deserve(?) (perhaps from <a href=#tsahr>tsahr<a link=clear> "go").

<font size=10 style=b>zith<font size=10 style=n> [ziT] (adj.) low.

<font size=10 style=b>zith-ah<font size=10 style=n> [ziTa] (adj.) lowest(?), less than(?).

<font size=10 style=b>zith-ah-<a href=#th>th<a link=clear><font size=10 style=n> [ziTaT] (n.) (lowest one, Least).

<font size=10 style=b>zithon<font size=10 style=n> [ziTon] (v.) (lower).

<font size=10 style=b>zo'e<font size=10 style=n> [zo'e] (n.) loss.

<font size=10 style=b>zoo<font size=10 style=n> [zU] (pron.) me.

<font size=10 style=b>zoodoo<font size=10 style=n> [zUDU] (v.) regret.

<font size=10 style=b>zuh<font size=10 style=n> [zu] (n.) end.

<font size=10 style=b>zuhnuh<font size=10 style=n> [zunu] (n.) ending.]]></translation>
            </element>
            <element name="DniDictED1">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictED1.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

English to D'ni Dictionary: A-F



<font size=12 style=n>Compiled by
Kh'reestrefah

Edited by
Korov'ev<PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>

                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb
<font size=12><PB>

<font style=b><p align=center>Sorting

<font size=12 style=b><p align=left>           <a href=#A>A<a link=clear>  <a href=#B>B<a link=clear>  <a href=#C>C<a link=clear>  <a href=#D>D<a link=clear>  <a href=#E>E<a link=clear>  <a href=#F>F<a link=clear>

<font size=10 style=n>Dnifont spellings are given in brackets: [Sora]. Tentative translations are marked with: (?).<PB><PB>

<a name=A><font size=12 style=b><p align=center>A<p align=left>

<font size=10 style=b>able<font size=10 style=n>: shin [Sin].

<font size=10 style=b>about (quantity)<font size=10 style=n>: blo [blo].

<font size=10 style=b>about (relation)<font size=10 style=n>: tso [xo].

<font size=10 style=b>above<font size=10 style=n>: p', pe [p', pe].

<font size=10 style=b>abyss<font size=10 style=n>: tsonot [xonot].

<font size=10 style=b>acid<font size=10 style=n>: bonoo [bonU].

<font size=10 style=b>acidic<font size=10 style=n>: bonooets [bonUex].

<font size=10 style=b>acquire<font size=10 style=n>: seen [sEn].

<font size=10 style=b>act (perform an action)<font size=10 style=n>: nahn [nan].

<font size=10 style=b>act (play a role)<font size=10 style=n>: fenges [fenges].

<font size=10 style=b>acting<font size=10 style=n>: fengestoy [fengestO].

<font size=10 style=b>action<font size=10 style=n>: nahntahv [nantav].

<font size=10 style=b>actor<font size=10 style=n>: fengestahn [fengestan].

<font size=10 style=b>actual<font size=10 style=n>: robot [robot].

<font size=10 style=b>add<font size=10 style=n>: chahg [cag].

<font size=10 style=b>again<font size=10 style=n>: d' [D'].

<font size=10 style=b>once again<font size=10 style=n>: preniv [preniv].

<font size=10 style=b>age<font size=10 style=n>: sev [sev].

<font size=10 style=b>all<font size=10 style=n>: biv [biv].

<font size=10 style=b>alright<font size=10 style=n>: sheemah [SEma].

<font size=10 style=b>always<font size=10 style=n>: tsahn [xan].

<font size=10 style=b>am (is, are, be)<font size=10 style=n>: ken [Ken].

<font size=10 style=b>am (is, are) ... -ing<font size=10 style=n>: do- [Do-].

<font size=10 style=b>among<font size=10 style=n>: te [te].

<font size=10 style=b>an<font size=10 style=n>: erth [erT].

<font size=10 style=b>ancient<font size=10 style=n>: oglahn [oglan].

<font size=10 style=b>and<font size=10 style=n>: gah [ga].

<font size=10 style=b>and the<font size=10 style=n>: gre- [gre-].

<font size=10 style=b>angel<font size=10 style=n>: sheeyah [SEya].

<font size=10 style=b>angle (unit of angular elevation)<font size=10 style=n>: toran [torån].

<font size=10 style=b>animal (burrowing)<font size=10 style=n>: tsaydortahn [xADortan].

<font size=10 style=b>animals (from Negilahn)<font size=10 style=n>: gahtsai, gipeli, kiri, nerim, oocha para, panuhdoy, pumi, reepah, tarpin shal, urwin.

<font size=10 style=b>animal (from Sameehn)<font size=10 style=n>: cheereetahn [cErEtan], undomesticated; cheereelay [cErElA], domesticated.

