            <element name="DniDictRE">
                <translation language="English"><![CDATA[<cover src="DniDictRE.hsm"><font size=12 style=b face=courier color=000000><margin right=56 left=56 top=40 bottom=40><PB><p align=center>

Rivenese to English Dictionary



<font size=12 style=n>Compiled by
Kh'reestrefah

Edited by
Korov'ev<PB><PB>

<font size=12 style=b><p align=center>Abbreviations<font size=10 style=n><p align=left>

                   adj: adjective
                   adv: adverb
                   art: article
                   aux: auxiliary
                    cf: compare
                  conj: conjunction
                determ: determinative
                   fut: future
                     n: noun
                   num: number
                  perf: perfect
                  pers: person
                  plur: plural
                  pref: prefix
                  prep: preposition
                  pres: present
                  prog: progressive
                  pron: pronoun
               quantif: quantifier
                  sing: singular
                  suff: suffix
                     v: verb<PB><PB><p align=left>

<a name=abirakin><font size=10 style=b>abi<font size=10 style=n> (v.) love: abirakin "I love you".

<font size=10 style=b>aimo<font size=10 style=n> (n.) woman.

<font size=10 style=b>ainela<font size=10 style=n> (n.) flower; girl.

<font size=10 style=b>aki<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) dangerous.

<font size=10 style=b>Allapo<font size=10 style=n> (n.) water pool.

<a name=allatwan><font size=10 style=b>Allatwan<font size=10 style=n> (n.) pool of stars (cf. <a href=#latai>latai<a link=clear> "star").

<font size=10 style=b>anarapo<font size=10 style=n> (v.) I praise: Gen anarapo "praise Gehn!" (lit. I praise Gehn).

<font size=10 style=b>atrapa<font size=10 style=n> (n.) arm; branch (of a tree).


<font size=10 style=b>babi<font size=10 style=n> (v.) cry, weep.

<font size=10 style=b>bela<font size=10 style=n> (n.) [day] (cf. <a href=#ohubela>ohubela<a link=clear> "celebration", <a href=#vrebela>vrebela<a link=clear> "yesterday", <a href=#yibela>yibela<a link=clear> "afternoon").

<font size=10 style=b>buku<font size=10 style=n> (n.) thing (generic).


<font size=10 style=b>cho<font size=10 style=n> (suff.) whoa, hey. Verbal suffix indicates speaker is surprised by the action.

<font size=10 style=b>choli<font size=10 style=n> (n.) sorrow, grief.


<font size=10 style=b>damai<font size=10 style=n> (v.) laugh.

<font size=10 style=b>droi<font size=10 style=n> (v.) carry.

<font size=10 style=b>duna<font size=10 style=n> (v.) dig; paddle, row.


<font size=10 style=b>edre<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) blue or green.

<font size=10 style=b>elari<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) beautiful.


<font size=10 style=b>fari<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) red.

<font size=10 style=b>fraita<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) trapped; captured.


<font size=10 style=b>kelarapo<font size=10 style=n> (v.) "I strike it".

<font size=10 style=b>kevisa<font size=10 style=n> (n.) mill stone, quern.

<font size=10 style=b>kowa<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) quiet, silent; a calm moment in the sea; a sunbreak.


<a name=latai><font size=10 style=b>latai<font size=10 style=n> (n.) star; beloved.

<font size=10 style=b>lopa<font size=10 style=n> (v.) shoot.

<font size=10 style=b>lopom<font size=10 style=n> (n.) heart.


<font size=10 style=b>-me<font size=10 style=n> (suff.) added to proverbial or gnomic statements ("everyone knows", "they say that").

<font size=10 style=b>mirimau<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) joy, happiness.

<font size=10 style=b>miyu<font size=10 style=n> (n.) story (usually spoken), an account of events.

<font size=10 style=b>mo<font size=10 style=n> (prep.) one; with.


<font size=10 style=b>-n<font size=10 style=n> (suff.) [you] (cf. <a href=#abirakin>abirakin<a link=clear> "I love you", <a href=#torilosan>torilosan<a link=clear> "they possibly discovered you").

<font size=10 style=b>navare<font size=10 style=n> (n.) frame, edge of an opening.

<font size=10 style=b>nefatai<font size=10 style=n> (v.) spark, ignite.

<font size=10 style=b>negen<font size=10 style=n> (v.) pour (lit. "to cause [to] run").


<a name=ohubela><font size=10 style=b>ohubela (n.) celebration (lit. "good-day").


<font size=10 style=b>palo<font size=10 style=n> (v.) stand; to be in a temporary state of.

<font size=10 style=b>poloiya<font size=10 style=n> (v.) escape.

<font size=10 style=b>puba<font size=10 style=n> (n.) lip; edge; shore.

<font size=10 style=b>pumeko<font size=10 style=n> (n.) whisper.


<font size=10 style=b>rahara<font size=10 style=n> (n.) anger.

<font size=10 style=b>rauno<font size=10 style=n> (adj.) strong in sensation (bright, loud, pungent, etc.); proud.

<font size=10 style=b>rekor<font size=10 style=n> (n.) Linking book (cf. D'ni rekor "the book").


<font size=10 style=b>sadago<font size=10 style=n> (n.) hide, leather, prepared skin of an animal.

<font size=10 style=b>safi<font size=10 style=n> (n.) song.

<font size=10 style=b>ser<font size=10 style=n> (v.) twist, coil.

<font size=10 style=b>serea<font size=10 style=n> (n.) grain.

<font size=10 style=b>shicho<font size=10 style=n> (n.) flying insect.

<font size=10 style=b>sraba<font size=10 style=n> (n.) leaf; page.

<font size=10 style=b>srain<font size=10 style=n> (n.) shadow.


<font size=10 style=b>take<font size=10 style=n> (v.) take.

<font size=10 style=b>tapomo<font size=10 style=n> (n.) window; eyepiece; doorway, opening; linking panel.

<font size=10 style=b>Tay<font size=10 style=n> (n.) Age of the Moiety after escaping from Riven.

<a name=tewan><font size=10 style=b>tewan<font size=10 style=n> (n.) clear daytime sky.

<font size=10 style=b>tis<font size=10 style=n> (v.) examine; read.

<a name=torilosan><font size=10 style=b>torilosan<font size=10 style=n> (v.) "they possibly discovered you".

<font size=10 style=b>tuweda<font size=10 style=n> (n.) memory.


<font size=10 style=b>ubin<font size=10 style=n> (n.) knot; joint; place where paths meet.

<font size=10 style=b>usoi<font size=10 style=n> (n.) bone.


<font size=10 style=b>vai<font size=10 style=n> (v.) want, desire.

<a name=vrebela><font size=10 style=b>vrebela<font size=10 style=n> (n.) yesterday.

<font size=10 style=b>vrirk<font size=10 style=n> (n.) sliver, a small piece; a moment of time.

<font size=10 style=b>vuten<font size=10 style=n> (n.) hide, skin (of an animal).


<font size=10 style=b>wahrk<font size=10 style=n> (n.) large, tusked, carnivorous animal that prowls the oceans on Riven.

<font size=10 style=b>wan<font size=10 style=n> (n.) sky(?); pool (?) (cf. <a href=#tewan>tewan<a link=clear> "clear daytime sky", wuwan "cloudy sky", <a href=#allatwan>Allatwan<a link=clear> "pool of stars").

<font size=10 style=b>wipe<font size=10 style=n> (n.) invader, interloper, unwanted guest.

<font size=10 style=b>wubo<font size=10 style=n> (n.) cloud.

<font size=10 style=b>wusifa<font size=10 style=n> (n.) prison; confinement.

<a name=wuwan><font size=10 style=b>wuwan<font size=10 style=n> (n.) cloudy sky.


<a name=yibela><font size=10 style=b>yibela<font size=10 style=n> (n.) uncertain period of time, approximately the length of an afternoon.

<font size=10 style=b>ytram<font size=10 style=n> (n.) froglike animal on Riven; Gehn captured the Ytrams and distilled them into a purified juice which he then smoked in his fire marble pipe.]]></translation>
            </element>
